  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a dynamic set at Wooly's in Des Moines, Iowa, on Saturday, July 16, 2022 [1][2]. This concert is the 344th of 467 archived shows for the band, following a previous performance at Off Broadway in STL on July 15, 2022 [2]. The recording, captured and transferred by Liz Hamilton, documents a 116-minute performance featuring 21 songs [1]. The setlist spans the band's extensive catalog, opening with “Aulon Raid” from *Songs for Pierre Chuvin* and “Color In Your Cheeks” from *All Hail West Texas* [1]. Notable rare moments include “Going to Kansas,” which had not been played in 39 archived shows, and “We Have Seen the Enemy,” absent from 90 prior archived performances [2]. The set continues with tracks like “Clemency for the Wizard King” and “Estate Sale Sign” [1]. The encore section is substantial, featuring “Let Me Bathe in Demonic Light,” “Broom People,” “Jenny,” “Song for Dennis Brown,” “This Year,” and “Up the Wolves” [1]. This recording is the only available documentation of this specific show, making it a valuable resource for fans [1]. The performance offers a comprehensive look at the band’s work, from early albums to later releases, all captured in a single, well-documented audio file [1][2].",
